Let me explain the difference between `Optional<@Nullable AccessoryServer>` and `Optional<AccessoryServer>`:

1. `Optional<AccessoryServer>`:
   - This means the Optional itself may be empty (null), but if it contains a value, that value will be a non-null `AccessoryServer`
   - When you call `get()` on this Optional, you're guaranteed to get a non-null `AccessoryServer` (or throw NoSuchElementException if empty)
   - This is the more common and recommended usage

2. `Optional<@Nullable AccessoryServer>`:
   - This means the Optional itself may be empty (null), AND if it contains a value, that value could also be null
